/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  cstr05_multiplicity  --  an ADIABATIC CSTR fed COLD, scanned for steady states.

  Eliminate the extents (at a fixed T the design equations are monotone) and
  what remains is ONE equation in the temperature:

      phi(T) = H_out(T) - H_in - Q_ext(T) = 0

  the textbook "heat generated equals heat removed".  The generation curve G(T)
  is a sigmoid (the rate saturates once the reactant is gone); the removal line
  R(T) = F cp (T - T_in) is straight (adiabatic: the only sink is the sensible
  heat that leaves with the product).  A straight line can cut a sigmoid THREE
  times: the extinguished state, an unstable middle state, and the ignited state
  -- IF the sigmoid is tall enough, i.e. IF the reaction releases enough heat.
  Choupo scans, finds them all, prints them, and reports the one nearest
  `T_guess`.  Change T_guess and the reactor moves to another branch -- when
  there is more than one.

  This case was written for exactly that: a 300 K feed, a negligible rate
  there, and an ignited branch reached by `T_guess`.  It no longer shows it.
  After the acetic-acid correction (docs/design/acetic-acid-latent-heat-closure.md)
  the liquid esterification is nearly thermoneutral (dH_rxn about -2.7 kJ/mol,
  where the engine used to print about -25.7), the complete-conversion
  adiabatic temperature is only 310.7 K, and G(T) is far too small to cut the
  removal line more than once: the scan finds ONE steady state, 300.04 K,
  whatever `T_guess` is (380 here, and the log says it landed from it).

  The original teaching point (multiplicity, ignition and extinction, a start-up
  procedure) needs a genuinely exothermic reaction: cstr08_furusawa_bistable runs
  one, with a measured rate law, and its scan finds three steady states.  No parameter was changed to recover the three states.
  The van Heerden construction itself is unchanged: the engine still scans,
  counts and prints every root it finds.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

units
(
    {
        name        reactor;
        type        cstr;
        in          feed;
        outputs     ( reactorOut );
        operation
        {
            V_R          0.005;         // m^3
            thermalMode  adiabatic;     // the removal line is pure sensible heat
            T_guess      380;            // declared start point of the Newton; with ONE
                                         //   steady state it lands on the same answer
                                         //   from 300 or from 380
        }
        reactions   ( esterification_etac );
    }
);
